  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Bulawayo - EC Urban Livelihoods Protection and Promotion Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project purpose is to improve the quality of life, livelihood security and reduce water borne diseases for approximately 3000 vunlnerable and poor household in the Peri-urban and Urban Plumtree District.This is to be acheived through a number of interventions which include improved water supply for domestic and human consumption at institutions( schools and hospitals) by borehole drilling and supply of water tanks, household urban waste management by training and supply of roller bins, PHHE( households and schools), Peer Education( youths and adolescence)establishment of Youth Freindly centres, HIV and AIDS prevention, support and mitigation, social cash transfers, income savings and lending and skills development for youths and adolesence in business and micro-lending.</narrative>
  </description>
